# Machine Learning in Crisis Scope
Crisis Scope incorporates AI-driven analytics to enhance disaster management and resource allocation. The ML models provide real-time impact assessment, urgency prediction, and optimization for food, aid, and rescue operations.

🛠️ ML Features:
Disaster Impact Prediction – Uses ML models to assess disaster severity and prioritize aid distribution.
Urgency-Based Prioritization – Automatically classifies food, aid, and rescue requests into Critical, High, Medium, and Low urgency levels.
Real-Time Demand Forecasting – Predicts future aid and food requests based on historical trends and real-time inputs.
Geospatial Heatmaps – Uses location data to generate heatmaps of affected regions, improving rescue planning.
Resource Optimization – Implements Linear Programming (LP) and Reinforcement Learning to allocate resources efficiently.
📊 Machine Learning Models Used
Feature	Model/Algorithm
Urgency Classification	Random Forest, XGBoost
Disaster Impact Prediction	CNN, LSTMs
Demand Forecasting	Time Series Analysis (ARIMA, LSTM)
Resource Optimization	Linear Programming (PuLP, SciPy)
Geospatial Analysis	K-Means Clustering, Heatmap Visualization
📂 ML Workflow>
Data Collection – Gathers request data from Firebase Firestore.
Data Preprocessing – Cleans and prepares data for ML models.
Feature Engineering – Extracts key parameters such as location, urgency level, and request trends.
Model Training & Evaluation – Trains AI models using scikit-learn, TensorFlow, and XGBoost.
Prediction & Prioritization – AI assigns urgency levels and forecasts resource demands.
Heatmap Generation – Displays affected regions in a real-time dashboard.
Model Deployment – Hosted on Firebase ML Kit for seamless integration.
⚙️ Tech Stack
Programming Language: Python
Libraries Used: TensorFlow, scikit-learn, XGBoost, Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, Seaborn
Visualization: Streamlit (for interactive ML dashboards)
Deployment:  FastAPI
